ed","decision_margin":-0.767,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The gate that decides whether to emit is the allowlist frozenset ... evaluated at the dispatch layer'","Plan: 'add the stderr emit at each allowlisted command's resolved-id point (which may be require_id ... or a command's own id-resolution arm)' and 'Confirm the exact per-command insertion point by reading the dispatch during implementation'","src/rebar/_lib_reads.py docstring: read path is 'alias-aware' — so cross_session_warning_for can resolve a raw id-form token itself, making per-arm resolved-id insertion unnecessary"],"finding":"The plan's emit mechanism is framed two incompatible ways: a SINGLE frozenset gate 'at the dispatch layer' AND an emit inserted 'at each allowlisted command's resolved-id point (require_id or a command's own id-resolution arm)' with a per-command 'confirm the insertion point during implementation'. The latter implies ~14 handler-arm insertion points (higher blast radius, more test surface) when a single dispatch-layer point that extracts the first positional token and hands the raw id to cross_session_warning_for achieves identical observable behavior — the detector's show_ticket read path is alias-aware (src/rebar/_lib_reads.py), so id resolution need not happen per-arm before the detector call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6d091e60184d3557","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope sections","norm_id":"nf71c1536d08e6463","priority":0.033,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer threads emit calls into transition/reopen/tag/set-file-impact/... arms, multiplying insertion points and per-arm tests","A future new single-ticket command is added but its arm is missed for the emit"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the emit as a single dispatch-layer step: after the frozenset membership check, extract the first non-flag positional from the command remainder (the primary id / link id1), pass